{"slug":"/students/subjects/biology/regulation/sensory-systems/","source":"students/subjects/biology/regulation/sensory-systems.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Sensory Systems - Biology","description":"","subject":"biology","body":"<!-- Header -->\n    <nav class=\"bg-white shadow-sm fixed top-0 w-full z-50\">\n        <div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4\">\n            <div class=\"flex justify-between h-16 items-center\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-center\">\n                    <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/regulation/\" class=\"text-purple-600 hover:text-purple-800 mr-4\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>\n                    </a>\n                    <h1 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900\">Sensory Systems</h1>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"flex items-center space-x-4\">\n                    <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 hidden sm:block\">\n                        Progress: <span id=\"progressPercent\">0%</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"w-24 sm:w-32 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full\">\n                        <div id=\"progressBar\" class=\"h-2 bg-purple-500 rounded-full transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <!-- Main Content -->\n    <main class=\"pt-20 pb-8 px-4 max-w-5xl mx-auto\">\n        <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n        <div class=\"bg-purple-50 border-l-4 border-purple-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Describe the structure and function of the human eye</li>\n                <li>• Explain how the ear detects sound and maintains balance</li>\n                <li>• Identify different types of sensory receptors</li>\n                <li>• Understand the mechanism of vision and hearing</li>\n                <li>• Explain common eye and ear defects</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 1: Introduction to Sensory Systems -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n                Introduction to Sensory Systems\n            </h2>\n            \n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\"><strong>Sensory systems</strong> allow organisms to detect changes in their environment (stimuli) and respond appropriately. They are essential for survival.</p>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-indigo-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-indigo-500 mb-4\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -sensor mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Types of Sensory Receptors</h4>\n                <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>Photoreceptors:</strong> Detect light (eyes)</li>\n                        <li><strong>Mechanoreceptors:</strong> Detect pressure, touch, sound (ears, skin)</li>\n                        <li><strong>Chemoreceptors:</strong> Detect chemicals (nose, tongue)</li>\n                    </ul>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>Thermoreceptors:</strong> Detect temperature changes (skin)</li>\n                        <li><strong>Proprioceptors:</strong> Detect body position (muscles, joints)</li>\n                        <li><strong>Nociceptors:</strong> Detect pain (throughout body)</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 2: The Human Eye -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n                The Human Eye\n            </h2>\n\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">The eye is the organ of sight. It detects light and converts it into electrical impulses that are sent to the brain.</p>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200 mb-4\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-3 text-center\"><span class=\"mi -eye mr-2\" data-mi=\"visibility\">visibility</span>Structure of the Eye</h4>\n                <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n                    <div>\n                        <h5 class=\"font-medium text-blue-600 mb-2\">Outer Layer (Protective)</h5>\n                        <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                            <li>• <strong>Sclera:</strong> White outer coat, protects eye</li>\n                            <li>• <strong>Cornea:</strong> Transparent front, refracts light</li>\n                            <li>• <strong>Conjunctiva:</strong> Thin membrane covering sclera</li>\n                        </ul>\n                    </div>\n                    <div>\n                        <h5 class=\"font-medium text-blue-600 mb-2\">Middle Layer (Vascular)</h5>\n                        <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                            <li>• <strong>Choroid:</strong> Contains blood vessels, dark pigment</li>\n                            <li>• <strong>Ciliary body:</strong> Controls lens shape</li>\n                            <li>• <strong>Iris:</strong> Colored part, controls pupil size</li>\n                        </ul>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-700 mb-2 text-center\">Lens</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Transparent, biconvex structure</li>\n                        <li>• Focuses light on retina</li>\n                        <li>• Changes shape for accommodation</li>\n                        <li>• Held by suspensory ligaments</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-700 mb-2 text-center\">Retina</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Inner light-sensitive layer</li>\n                        <li>• Contains photoreceptors</li>\n                        <li>• Rods: dim light, black/white</li>\n                        <li>• Cones: bright light, color vision</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2 text-center\">Other Parts</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• <strong>Pupil:</strong> Hole in iris, lets in light</li>\n                        <li>• <strong>Aqueous humor:</strong> Fluid in front</li>\n                        <li>• <strong>Vitreous humor:</strong> Jelly behind lens</li>\n                        <li>• <strong>Optic nerve:</strong> Sends signals to brain</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -route mr-2\" data-mi=\"route\">route</span>Pathway of Light Through Eye:</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Light → Cornea → Aqueous humor → Pupil → Lens → Vitreous humor → Retina → Optic nerve → Brain</p>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 3: Vision Mechanism -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n                How We See\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-orange-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -adjust mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Pupil Reflex</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">The iris controls the size of the pupil to regulate light entry:</p>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• <strong>Bright light:</strong> Circular muscles contract → Pupil constricts → Less light enters</li>\n                        <li>• <strong>Dim light:</strong> Radial muscles contract → Pupil dilates → More light enters</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-teal-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-teal-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-teal-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -focus mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Accommodation</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">The lens changes shape to focus on objects at different distances:</p>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• <strong>Distant objects:</strong> Ciliary muscles relax → Lens becomes thinner → Less refraction</li>\n                        <li>• <strong>Near objects:</strong> Ciliary muscles contract → Lens becomes thicker → More refraction</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -brain mr-2\" data-mi=\"psychology\">psychology</span>Formation of Image</h4>\n                <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                    <li>• Light rays are refracted by cornea and lens</li>\n                    <li>• Image formed on retina is <strong>real, inverted, and smaller</strong> than the object</li>\n                    <li>• Photoreceptors convert light to electrical impulses</li>\n                    <li>• Optic nerve transmits impulses to visual cortex in brain</li>\n                    <li>• Brain interprets the image correctly (right side up)</li>\n                </ul>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 4: Eye Defects -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n                Eye Defects and Correction\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-700 mb-2 text-center\"><span class=\"mi -glasses mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Short-sightedness (Myopia)</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Cause:</strong> Eyeball too long or lens too curved</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Problem:</strong> Light focuses in front of retina</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Can see:</strong> Near objects clearly</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Cannot see:</strong> Distant objects clearly</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Correction:</strong> <span class=\"text-red-600 font-medium\">Concave lens (diverging)</span></p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2 text-center\"><span class=\"mi -glasses mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Long-sightedness (Hyperopia)</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Cause:</strong> Eyeball too short or lens too flat</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Problem:</strong> Light focuses behind retina</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Can see:</strong> Distant objects clearly</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Cannot see:</strong> Near objects clearly</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Correction:</strong> <span class=\"text-blue-600 font-medium\">Convex lens (converging)</span></p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2 text-center\"><span class=\"mi -cloud mr-2\" data-mi=\"cloud\">cloud</span>Other Defects</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-2\">\n                        <li><strong>Astigmatism:</strong> Uneven cornea → blurred vision at all distances</li>\n                        <li><strong>Presbyopia:</strong> Loss of lens elasticity with age → difficulty reading</li>\n                        <li><strong>Cataract:</strong> Cloudy lens → leads to blindness</li>\n                        <li><strong>Glaucoma:</strong> Increased pressure in eye → damages optic nerve</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 5: The Human Ear -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n                The Human Ear\n            </h2>\n\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">The ear has two main functions: <strong>hearing</strong> and <strong>balance</strong>. It detects sound waves and head position.</p>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-amber-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-amber-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -ear-listen mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Outer Ear</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>Pinna:</strong> Visible part, collects sound waves</li>\n                        <li><strong>Ear canal:</strong> Directs sound to eardrum</li>\n                        <li><strong>Earwax:</strong> Traps dust, protects ear</li>\n                        <li><strong>Eardrum (tympanum):</strong> Vibrates with sound</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-rose-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-rose-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-rose-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -drum mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Middle Ear</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>Ossicles:</strong> Three tiny bones</li>\n                        <li>- Malleus (hammer)</li>\n                        <li>- Incus (anvil)</li>\n                        <li>- Stapes (stirrup)</li>\n                        <li><strong>Eustachian tube:</strong> Equalizes pressure</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-cyan-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-cyan-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-cyan-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -water mr-2\" data-mi=\"water\">water</span>Inner Ear</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>Cochlea:</strong> Spiral organ for hearing</li>\n                        <li>- Contains hair cells</li>\n                        <li>- Converts vibrations to impulses</li>\n                        <li><strong>Semicircular canals:</strong> Balance</li>\n                        <li><strong>Vestibule:</strong> Static balance</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -route mr-2\" data-mi=\"route\">route</span>Pathway of Sound Through Ear:</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Sound waves → Pinna → Ear canal → Eardrum → Ossicles → Oval window → Cochlea (fluid) → Hair cells → Auditory nerve → Brain</p>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 6: Hearing and Balance -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">6</span>\n                Hearing and Balance Mechanisms\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -volume-up mr-2\" data-mi=\"volume_up\">volume_up</span>Hearing Mechanism</h4>\n                    <ol class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-2\">\n                        <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-5 h-5 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2\">1</span>Sound waves are collected by pinna</li>\n                        <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-5 h-5 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2\">2</span>Waves travel through ear canal to eardrum</li>\n                        <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-5 h-5 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2\">3</span>Eardrum vibrates at same frequency as sound</li>\n                        <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-5 h-5 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2\">4</span>Vibrations amplified by ossicles (22×)</li>\n                        <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-5 h-5 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2\">5</span>Oval window transmits to cochlear fluid</li>\n                        <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-5 h-5 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2\">6</span>Hair cells in cochlea detect vibrations</li>\n                        <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-5 h-5 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2\">7</span>Impulses sent via auditory nerve to brain</li>\n                    </ol>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -balance-scale mr-2\" data-mi=\"balance\">balance</span>Balance Mechanism</h4>\n                    <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                        <div>\n                            <p class=\"font-medium text-blue-600\">Semicircular Canals (Dynamic Balance)</p>\n                            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Three canals at right angles, filled with fluid and hair cells. Detect rotational movements of head.</p>\n                        </div>\n                        <div>\n                            <p class=\"font-medium text-blue-600\">Vestibule (Static Balance)</p>\n                            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Contains utricle and saccule with otoliths (calcium carbonate crystals). Detect head position relative to gravity.</p>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>How it works:</strong> When head moves, fluid moves and bends hair cells. This sends impulses to the cerebellum, which coordinates muscle responses to maintain balance.</p>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 7: Other Senses -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">7</span>\n                Other Sensory Systems\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-pink-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-pink-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-pink-700 mb-2 text-center\"><span class=\"mi -nose mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Smell (Olfaction)</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Chemoreceptors in nasal cavity</li>\n                        <li>• Detect airborne chemicals</li>\n                        <li>• Olfactory nerve to brain</li>\n                        <li>• Closely linked to taste</li>\n                        <li>• Can detect ~10,000 different smells</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-orange-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-700 mb-2 text-center\"><span class=\"mi -tongue mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Taste (Gustation)</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Taste buds on tongue papillae</li>\n                        <li>• Chemoreceptors detect dissolved chemicals</li>\n                        <li>• 5 basic tastes: sweet, sour, salty, bitter, umami</li>\n                        <li>• Different parts of tongue detect different tastes</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-amber-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-amber-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2 text-center\"><span class=\"mi -hand-paper mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Touch (Skin)</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Various receptors in skin</li>\n                        <li>• Detect pressure, touch, temperature, pain</li>\n                        <li>• Different body parts have different sensitivity</li>\n                        <li>• Fingertips most sensitive</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 8: Video -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">8</span>\n                Video: The Eye and Ear\n            </h2>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                <div class=\"video-container\">\n                    <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/0VO033bGewY\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 9: Practice Problems -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-purple-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n                Practice Questions\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. Explain the role of the ciliary muscles in accommodation.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            When viewing <strong>near objects</strong>: Ciliary muscles contract, reducing tension on suspensory ligaments, allowing the lens to become thicker (more convex) and increase refraction.<br><br>\n                            When viewing <strong>distant objects</strong>: Ciliary muscles relax, increasing tension on suspensory ligaments, pulling the lens thinner (less convex) and decreasing refraction.\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. What type of lens is used to correct short-sightedness and why?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            A <strong>concave (diverging) lens</strong> is used to correct short-sightedness (myopia).<br><br>\n                            In myopia, light focuses in front of the retina because the eyeball is too long or the lens is too powerful. A concave lens diverges (spreads out) the light rays before they enter the eye, so they focus correctly on the retina instead of in front of it.\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Describe the role of the ossicles in hearing.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            The <strong>ossicles</strong> (malleus, incus, stapes) are three tiny bones in the middle ear that:\n                            <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside mt-1\">\n                                <li><strong>Amplify</strong> vibrations from the eardrum by about 22 times</li>\n                                <li><strong>Transmit</strong> vibrations from the eardrum to the oval window</li>\n                                <li>Overcome the impedance mismatch between air and cochlear fluid</li>\n                                <li>Protect the inner ear from loud sounds (acoustic reflex)</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. How do the semicircular canals detect rotational movement?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            The three semicircular canals are positioned at right angles to each other. When the head rotates:\n                            <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside mt-1 space-y-1\">\n                                <li>The fluid (endolymph) inside the canals lags behind due to inertia</li>\n                                <li>This relative movement bends the hair cells in the ampulla</li>\n                                <li>Bent hair cells trigger nerve impulses</li>\n                                <li>Different canals detect rotation in different planes (horizontal, vertical, torsional)</li>\n                                <li>Information is sent to the cerebellum for balance coordination</li>\n                            </ol>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-50 to-pink-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-purple-200 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n                <li>• Eye: Cornea and lens refract light; retina contains rods (dim light) and cones (color)</li>\n                <li>• Accommodation: Lens changes shape to focus on near/distant objects</li>\n                <li>• Myopia (short-sighted): Concave lens correction; Hyperopia (long-sighted): Convex lens</li>\n                <li>• Ear: Ossicles amplify sound; Cochlea detects sound; Semicircular canals detect balance</li>\n                <li>• All sensory systems convert stimuli to electrical impulses sent to the brain</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Navigation -->\n        <div class=\"flex justify-between items-center mt-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/regulation/nervous-coordination/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900\">\n                <span class=\"mi -chevron-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_left\">chevron_left</span>Previous\n            </a>\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/regulation/hormonal-coordination/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 bg-purple-500 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-purple-600\">\n                Next: Hormonal Coordination<span class=\"mi -chevron-right ml-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_right\">chevron_right</span>\n            </a>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    \n\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"bg-gray-50 min-h-screen","bodyStyle":"","css":["@keyframes fade-in-up {\n            from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); }\n            to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }\n        }\n        .animate-fade-in-up { animation: fade-in-up 0.5s ease-out forwards; }\n        .section-card {\n            background: white;\n            border-radius: 12px;\n            padding: 1.5rem;\n            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;\n            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\n            border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\n        }\n        .video-container {\n            position: relative;\n            width: 100%;\n            padding-bottom: 56.25%;\n            height: 0;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            background: #f9fafb;\n        }\n        .video-container iframe {\n            position: absolute;\n            top: 0; left: 0;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n            border: none;\n        }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}